The structure-independent test is decisive for the inventory: the Pbam Mn₂WO₅ lattice drops Rwp to 9.46% while holding the two accepted phases fixed, so its allowed reflections cover the coherent residual family. The remaining problem is now structure-factor recovery—finding physical Pbam coordinates that reproduce those extracted intensities—not phase discovery.

