A more defensible route is now clear: the indexed metric and stoichiometry point to a Mn₂BiO₅-type Mn₂WO₅ framework, but the diffraction requires symmetry lowering from Pbam. I’m fitting the split heavy-atom sublattice in its inversion subgroup, using Le Bail intensities only as a structure-solution aid and enforcing ordinary Mn–O/W–O geometry.

