Texture tests are informative: wolframite shows no meaningful orientation, while the indexed Mn₂WO₅ phase strongly favors March–Dollase [110] (ratio ≈0.753), lowering Rwp to 15.304%. I’m repeating that branch from its checkpoint to verify convergence and then checking whether the weaker WO₃ [010] effect survives alongside it.

All coherent residual peaks remain at the accepted Mn₂WO₅ reflection positions; the remaining error is intensity-centered, not an unindexed family. The complete checkpoint is converged and contact-free, so I’m freezing it as `final.gpx` and invoking the prescribed staged coordinate polish exactly once now.

